# Ref-shipped data migrations, one line per migration:
#
#   <apply-script> <check-script>        (both relative to the checkout root)
#
# The SAME list drives BOTH runner calls of a rollout: install-artifact.sh
# (rehearsal, on the standby's own database) and switch.sh --rebase (the
# restored snapshot, at cutover). ONE parser reads it —
# tools/deploy/run_migrations.py — never a shell loop: the 2026-09-24 silent
# skip was a `while read` that dropped a final line carrying no trailing
# newline, and a shell loop cannot refuse an empty list.
#
# apply-script contract: `<python> <apply> --db <db>` is a READ-ONLY dry-run
#   report; `--apply --backup --backup-path <p> --verify` writes. An apply that
#   had NOTHING to write prints `no-write: <why>` and exits 0: the runner then
#   requires no backup (nothing was written to protect) and still runs the check.
#   The statement is required, not implied — an apply that leaves no backup and
#   says nothing is a FAILED apply. Without it, an idempotent no-op (the
#   already-split database a fresh box restores from the seed) fails a rollout
#   that has nothing to migrate.
# check-script contract: `<python> <check> --db <db>` opens the DB read-only and
#   exits 0 iff the migration's effect is complete. A separate program from the
#   apply, so it cannot vouch for the code that just wrote.
#
# Adding a migration = shipping both scripts + one line here. A blank or
# comments-only list is REFUSED by the runner (zero migrations cannot be
# reported as "0 applied+checked, 0 failed").
# ORDER IS PART OF THE CONTRACT. backfill_person_ids first, split_node_results
# second. The backfill rewrites the record and writes it through
# dag/persistence.py, which mirrors the legacy `result_json` blob while that
# column exists; the split reads that blob to fill the per-field columns and
# then DROPS the column. Reversed, the backfill's changes would land in the
# split columns only, and the split would overwrite them from the stale blob.
scripts/backfill_person_ids.py scripts/backfill_person_ids.check.py
scripts/split_node_results.py scripts/split_node_results.check.py
